WEBVTT

1
00:01:13.157 --> 00:01:14.550
All aboard, girls!

2
00:01:15.943 --> 00:01:17.727
Bye!

3
00:01:55.112 --> 00:01:57.200
- Welcome home, honey!
- Hi, Daddy!

4
00:01:57.201 --> 00:01:58.332
Hi, Mom!

5
00:01:58.333 --> 00:02:00.073
- Mom!
- Hi!

6
00:02:00.074 --> 00:02:02.380
Hi!

7
00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.687
Wait.
Did you get taller?

8
00:02:05.688 --> 00:02:07.471
- Yes, I did.
- Wow.

9
00:02:07.472 --> 00:02:08.995
So good. Okay.
Oh, here it is.

10
00:02:08.996 --> 00:02:10.518
- Let's get your trunk.
- Yes.

11
00:02:10.519 --> 00:02:13.260
I double-parked the car
and they're already mad at me.

12
00:02:13.261 --> 00:02:15.175
- What car?
- Oh, we bought a car.

13
00:02:15.176 --> 00:02:16.741
- We bought got a car?
- Yeah!

14
00:02:16.742 --> 00:02:18.439
- What for?
- I'll explain later.

15
00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:19.744
It's that big blue one right over there.

16
00:02:19.745 --> 00:02:21.224
In the middle of the road.

17
00:02:21.225 --> 00:02:22.747
- Hey, lady, you kidding me?
- Sorry!

18
00:02:22.748 --> 00:02:23.923
- Sorry, we're going. One second.
- There's my girl!

19
00:02:23.924 --> 00:02:25.620
Grandma!

20
00:02:25.621 --> 00:02:27.535
Ah!

21
00:02:27.536 --> 00:02:30.146
- Oh, God, I missed you!
- Me, too!

22
00:02:30.147 --> 00:02:31.713
Lady, you can't stop in the
middle of the street. Let's go!

23
00:02:31.714 --> 00:02:33.062
- I'm sorry. Promise, two more seconds.
- Come on, lady.

24
00:02:33.063 --> 00:02:34.194
Welcome home gift.

25
00:02:34.195 --> 00:02:35.804
- Oh, you made this?
- From scratch.

26
00:02:35.805 --> 00:02:37.066
- Aw!
- It's cashmere.

27
00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:38.154
I did everything

28
00:02:38.155 --> 00:02:39.677
but shave the goat.

29
00:02:39.678 --> 00:02:41.114
- Margaret! Can you just...
- Let's go, ladies.

30
00:02:41.115 --> 00:02:43.507
I'm so sorry.
Yeah, get the bottom there.

31
00:02:43.508 --> 00:02:45.770
- Okay. You got it.
- Here we go. Okay.

32
00:02:45.771 --> 00:02:47.468
- Right on, girls.
- All right, here we go.

33
00:02:47.469 --> 00:02:49.296
- Oh, God.
- Heavy.

34
00:02:49.297 --> 00:02:50.645
Watch out for the...

35
00:02:50.646 --> 00:02:53.039
- Watch out for the bike.
- Oh, God.

36
00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.779
Here we go.

37
00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.999
Whoa, whoa, whoa, hey.
I would've done it.

38
00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.218
Oh, hi!

39
00:02:58.219 --> 00:03:00.133
I would've done it.
Please, please.

40
00:03:00.134 --> 00:03:02.352
- Oh, my God. Amazing.
- We got it.

41
00:03:02.353 --> 00:03:04.789
- Dad!
- Hello! Oh, my goodness!

42
00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:07.227
- I'm so glad to see you.
- Me, too!

43
00:03:07.228 --> 00:03:08.663
Look at that!
What happened?

44
00:03:08.664 --> 00:03:10.404
- So, how was camp?
- It was amazing.

45
00:03:10.405 --> 00:03:11.492
- So, you were in a play?
- Yep!

46
00:03:11.493 --> 00:03:13.494
Oh, my God.
That's incredible.

47
00:03:13.495 --> 00:03:14.930
- What are those boxes for?
- Don't worry about that.

48
00:03:14.931 --> 00:03:16.018
I want to hear more about camp.

49
00:03:16.019 --> 00:03:17.193
What else did you learn?

50
00:03:17.194 --> 00:03:18.754
- What else did you do?
- You're moving.

51
00:03:20.458 --> 00:03:21.719
- What?
- Really, Mom?

52
00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.374
- Sylvia. You promised.
- Oh, wow.

53
00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:24.984
We're moving?

54
00:03:24.985 --> 00:03:26.333
Look, it's...
Look, we we're...

55
00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:27.856
She saw the boxes.

56
00:03:27.857 --> 00:03:29.249
- She was putting it together.
- I don't think she was.

57
00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:30.641
- We're moving?
- Okay.

58
00:03:30.642 --> 00:03:32.165
Just...

59
00:03:32.166 --> 00:03:34.210
Look, we wanted you to settle in

60
00:03:34.211 --> 00:03:35.864
before we sprung the news.

61
00:03:35.865 --> 00:03:38.040
But, um, your dad got his promotion.

62
00:03:38.041 --> 00:03:40.347
- Yeah. Isn't that great?
- And we found

63
00:03:40.348 --> 00:03:41.435
- this great house.
- Oh, the best house.

64
00:03:41.436 --> 00:03:42.914
- The best house.
- Where?

65
00:03:42.915 --> 00:03:45.526
Well, that's the thing.
We got really lucky. And...

66
00:03:45.527 --> 00:03:47.572
- New Jersey.
- Ah...

67
00:03:49.009 --> 00:03:51.358
- New Jersey?
- I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

68
00:03:51.359 --> 00:03:53.316
I said I'd stay out of it.

69
00:03:53.317 --> 00:03:54.970
We're leaving New York?

70
00:03:54.971 --> 00:03:57.016
Barely leaving New York.

71
00:03:57.017 --> 00:03:58.843
It's just on the other side of the river.

72
00:03:58.844 --> 00:04:00.063
But...

73
00:04:01.369 --> 00:04:03.326
But we're happy here.
We don't need to move.

74
00:04:03.327 --> 00:04:05.633
No, we don't need to move
but we want to move. Right?

75
00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:07.026
I don't.

76
00:04:07.027 --> 00:04:10.029
I'll have to leave all of my friends

77
00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:11.856
and change schools

78
00:04:11.857 --> 00:04:14.033
and I'll never see Grandma anymore.

79
00:04:14.034 --> 00:04:15.686
That is not true.

80
00:04:15.687 --> 00:04:17.384
Look, you're going to keep
all your friends here

81
00:04:17.385 --> 00:04:20.822
and you're going to make more friends.
And listen to this.

82
00:04:20.823 --> 00:04:22.216
I'm not going to work anymore.

83
00:04:23.304 --> 00:04:25.479
Do you know what that means?

84
00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:28.047
That means that I'm not going
to be gone all the time.

85
00:04:28.048 --> 00:04:30.658
Running from class to class.

86
00:04:30.659 --> 00:04:33.705
God. Do you know how bad I felt about that?

87
00:04:35.055 --> 00:04:37.057
But you love teaching art.

88
00:04:38.275 --> 00:04:42.626
Oh, yeah.
Yeah, I do, I do, but...

89
00:04:42.627 --> 00:04:45.369
But this is,
this is our opportunity.

90
00:04:46.457 --> 00:04:48.023
I'll be home now.

91
00:04:48.024 --> 00:04:51.766
I can be home with you every single day.

92
00:04:51.767 --> 00:04:53.376
I'll get involved at your school,

93
00:04:53.377 --> 00:04:55.422
just like all your friends' moms.

94
00:04:55.423 --> 00:04:58.686
And we'll have family dinners
and I'll learn to cook.

95
00:05:00.732 --> 00:05:01.951
I know it's a lot.

96
00:05:03.213 --> 00:05:04.910
Can you just try to believe us?

97
00:05:07.957 --> 00:05:09.045
Yeah.

98
00:05:11.003 --> 00:05:12.004
Mmm.

99
00:05:13.702 --> 00:05:15.833
I love you so much.
Come here.

100
00:05:15.834 --> 00:05:20.055
Come here. You, too.
And you, Sylvia.

101
00:05:20.056 --> 00:05:22.449
- Sylvia. Come on.
- Come on, Mom. Come on.

102
00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:25.016
Come on.
You know you want to.

103
00:05:25.017 --> 00:05:26.235
Faster.

104
00:05:26.236 --> 00:05:28.716
Okay, okay,
I'm coming, I'm coming.

105
00:05:28.717 --> 00:05:30.849
- There we go.
- Oh, my darling.

106
00:05:32.068 --> 00:05:33.982
I'm never going to see you again.

107
00:05:33.983 --> 00:05:35.549
Oh, Jesus.

108
00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:38.682
- Wow.
- So dramatic all the time.

109
00:05:38.683 --> 00:05:40.031
What are you taking her over there

110
00:05:40.032 --> 00:05:41.424
with the schmucks and the condos

111
00:05:41.425 --> 00:05:42.773
on the other side of the Hudson?

112
00:05:42.774 --> 00:05:43.861
But we're not going to be in a condo.

113
00:05:43.862 --> 00:05:45.254
And those mafia diners,

114
00:05:45.255 --> 00:05:46.473
where they shoot each other...

115
00:06:07.886 --> 00:06:09.758
God...

116
00:06:22.336 --> 00:06:23.511
God?

117
00:06:28.516 --> 00:06:29.952
Are you there, God?

118
00:06:31.214 --> 00:06:35.566
It's me... Margaret Simon.

119
00:06:38.526 --> 00:06:39.701
Um...

120
00:06:42.312 --> 00:06:44.184
I just wanted... Well...

121
00:06:46.055 --> 00:06:48.492
First, I've, I've heard a lot
of great things about you.

122
00:06:52.714 --> 00:06:55.106
I don't want to move.

123
00:06:55.107 --> 00:06:57.806
I've never lived anywhere
but the city, and...

124
00:06:58.937 --> 00:07:01.243
I... I don't want to do this.

125
00:07:01.244 --> 00:07:03.419
Please, I'm begging you.

126
00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:06.031
Just please, just stop
this move from happening.

127
00:07:10.732 --> 00:07:14.214
Um, if...
if you can't do that...

128
00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:20.394
Just please don't let
New Jersey be too horrible.

129
00:07:52.382 --> 00:07:55.080
- You're gonna have to hurry up, all right?
- Okay, Dad!

130
00:08:17.407 --> 00:08:19.888
Okay, you.
You need some light.

131
00:08:22.151 --> 00:08:24.284
Oh, God.

132
00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:26.894
They smell bad?

133
00:08:26.895 --> 00:08:28.809
Oh, they don't smell good, honey.

134
00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:32.421
- You're going to be there very soon.
- Believe me.

135
00:08:32.422 --> 00:08:33.597
I'll get it.

136
00:08:36.296 --> 00:08:37.600
I already know your name's Margaret

137
00:08:37.601 --> 00:08:38.862
and you're in sixth grade.

138
00:08:38.863 --> 00:08:40.429
The real estate agent sent out,

139
00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:42.257
like, a tiny flyer about you
to the whole neighborhood.

140
00:08:42.258 --> 00:08:44.129
It was, like, this big
and it had your picture.

141
00:08:44.913 --> 00:08:46.522
Oh, okay.

142
00:08:46.523 --> 00:08:48.742
I'm Nancy.
I'm in sixth grade, too.

143
00:08:48.743 --> 00:08:49.917
Do you want to come over to my house

144
00:08:49.918 --> 00:08:51.527
and run under the sprinklers with me?

145
00:08:51.528 --> 00:08:53.964
Oh. I don't know.

146
00:08:53.965 --> 00:08:55.662
You don't know?

147
00:08:55.663 --> 00:08:59.492
Oh, no, no, no.
I just mean I'll have to ask.

148
00:08:59.493 --> 00:09:01.277
Um, just a second.

149
00:09:02.844 --> 00:09:04.148
- Mom?
- Yeah?

150
00:09:04.149 --> 00:09:05.672
There's a girl from the neighborhood

151
00:09:05.673 --> 00:09:07.500
who asked if I could go
under the sprinklers with her.

152
00:09:07.501 --> 00:09:09.893
Oh, that's great.
Yeah.

153
00:09:09.894 --> 00:09:11.417
I need my bathing suit.

154
00:09:11.418 --> 00:09:12.809
Good luck finding it in here.

155
00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:14.986
That's all right.
She can borrow one of mine.

156
00:09:16.423 --> 00:09:18.467
Oh, hello.

157
00:09:18.468 --> 00:09:21.165
Nancy Wheeler.
I live in the bigger house up the street.

158
00:09:21.166 --> 00:09:22.211
Come on, let's go.

159
00:09:28.739 --> 00:09:30.740
Whose class are you in at Delano?

160
00:09:30.741 --> 00:09:32.003
Um...

161
00:09:33.091 --> 00:09:35.092
The letter said "Room 18."

162
00:09:35.093 --> 00:09:37.356
I'm in room 18, too!

163
00:09:37.357 --> 00:09:38.748
We were supposed to have Miss Phipps,

164
00:09:38.749 --> 00:09:40.794
but she ran off
with some guy to California,

165
00:09:40.795 --> 00:09:42.143
so we're going to get a new teacher now.

166
00:09:42.144 --> 00:09:44.364
Come on.
Room's upstairs.

167
00:09:49.586 --> 00:09:50.586
Voila.

168
00:09:52.154 --> 00:09:53.373
My bathing suit's over here.

169
00:09:55.679 --> 00:09:57.419
Um...

170
00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:59.943
- Here. It's clean.
- Thanks.

171
00:09:59.944 --> 00:10:02.382
- Where should I change?
- What's wrong with here?

172
00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:07.342
Nothing.
I don't mind if you don't mind.

173
00:10:07.343 --> 00:10:08.823
Why would I mind?

174
00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:24.926
You're still flat.

175
00:10:25.622 --> 00:10:26.666
Um...

176
00:10:26.667 --> 00:10:29.104
Well, I'm already growing.
See?

177
00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:31.890
I'm going to have a pretty big chest.

178
00:10:35.023 --> 00:10:36.415
You know, coming from New York,

179
00:10:36.416 --> 00:10:38.417
I thought you'd be a lot more grown up.

180
00:10:38.418 --> 00:10:39.549
Have you ever kissed a boy?

181
00:10:40.898 --> 00:10:43.596
You mean, like, really kiss?
Like, on the lips?

182
00:10:43.597 --> 00:10:45.425
Yeah.
Have you?

183
00:10:46.208 --> 00:10:48.209
Not exactly.

184
00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:50.951
Neither have I,
but I practice a lot.

185
00:10:50.952 --> 00:10:52.432
You want to see?

186
00:11:13.757 --> 00:11:15.149
What?

187
00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:16.324
- Sorry.
- You have to practice

188
00:11:16.325 --> 00:11:18.066
or else you won't be a good kisser.

189
00:11:19.676 --> 00:11:20.938
Ready to go?

190
00:11:21.852 --> 00:11:22.939
Sure.

191
00:11:24.115 --> 00:11:25.987
Follow the leader.

192
00:11:27.684 --> 00:11:28.859
Yeah, watch me.

193
00:11:42.177 --> 00:11:43.831
- I'm a supermodel.
- Okay.

194
00:11:49.053 --> 00:11:51.664
- Evan, you stupid idiot!
- I'm sorry.

195
00:11:51.665 --> 00:11:53.187
You're such a great model, by the way.

196
00:11:53.188 --> 00:11:54.275
Who are they?

197
00:11:54.276 --> 00:11:55.450
It's my dumb brother

198
00:11:55.451 --> 00:11:56.495
- and his stupid friend.
- Hey.

199
00:11:56.496 --> 00:11:58.409
- Mom!
- That was uncalled for.

200
00:11:58.410 --> 00:11:59.455
Who are you?

201
00:12:00.674 --> 00:12:03.110
Margaret.
Um, we moved in down the street.

202
00:12:03.111 --> 00:12:04.633
Oh, so you're the new people?

203
00:12:04.634 --> 00:12:06.200
Ask your dad if he wants me
to cut the lawn.

204
00:12:06.201 --> 00:12:07.636
Five bucks, and I trim, too.

205
00:12:07.637 --> 00:12:09.987
Evan!
Get over here right now!

206
00:12:10.945 --> 00:12:12.250
- I got to go.
- Dude...

207
00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:22.870
Got to get us more birdseed.

208
00:12:23.653 --> 00:12:25.480
Yeah.

209
00:12:25.481 --> 00:12:28.527
My name's Moose. Moose Freed.
I live down the street, too.

210
00:12:28.528 --> 00:12:29.572
Um...

211
00:12:30.921 --> 00:12:32.095
Yeah, but don't forget to ask your dad

212
00:12:32.096 --> 00:12:33.620
about the lawn thingy.

213
00:12:34.359 --> 00:12:36.013
Yeah.
I won't.

214
00:12:37.406 --> 00:12:39.059
Oh, now I got to go see Evan.

215
00:12:43.499 --> 00:12:45.108
Sorry you got stuck with Moose.

216
00:12:45.109 --> 00:12:46.981
Oh, that's okay.

217
00:12:47.851 --> 00:12:50.374
Anyways, listen, Margaret.

218
00:12:50.375 --> 00:12:52.899
I've decided I want you
to join my secret club.

219
00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:55.379
There's three of us
and I'm letting in one more.

220
00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:56.598
But you can't wear socks

221
00:12:56.599 --> 00:12:58.119
or else the others might not want you.

222
00:12:58.688 --> 00:12:59.689
Oh.

223
00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:01.821
See you later.

224
00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:07.697
<i>Are you there, God?
It's me, Margaret, again.</i>

225
00:13:13.485 --> 00:13:15.095
It's the first day of school tomorrow.

226
00:13:15.096 --> 00:13:16.662
I met this girl, Nancy.

227
00:13:16.663 --> 00:13:19.055
I don't really know if she liked me.

228
00:13:19.056 --> 00:13:24.540
I think she just expected me
to be different or something.

229
00:13:26.368 --> 00:13:30.066
Anyway, well,
it did get me thinking.

230
00:13:30.067 --> 00:13:33.504
Maybe it is time for...

231
00:13:33.505 --> 00:13:37.247
things to be happening around here?

232
00:13:38.946 --> 00:13:39.990
Come in.

233
00:13:41.165 --> 00:13:43.558
Look.

234
00:13:43.559 --> 00:13:44.951
<i>Anyway, just think
about what I mentioned.</i>

235
00:13:44.952 --> 00:13:46.126
It was in with the bathroom stuff.

236
00:13:46.127 --> 00:13:47.606
I found this, too,
if you need it.

237
00:13:47.607 --> 00:13:48.694
<i>Thanks, God.</i>

238
00:13:48.695 --> 00:13:50.478
- Thanks, Mom.
- Mmm-hmm.

239
00:13:52.786 --> 00:13:54.830
Oh, wow, look at you.

240
00:13:54.831 --> 00:13:57.485
Are you ready for your first day?
How you feeling?

241
00:13:57.486 --> 00:13:59.313
It's going to be great, right?

242
00:13:59.314 --> 00:14:02.838
And if it's not great,
first days don't count anyways.

243
00:14:02.839 --> 00:14:04.144
- Right?
- Exactly.

244
00:14:04.145 --> 00:14:05.493
- All right. See you later.
- Bye!

245
00:14:05.494 --> 00:14:08.191
- Bye!
- Did I not unpack your socks?

246
00:14:08.192 --> 00:14:11.064
Oh, um, uh...

247
00:14:11.065 --> 00:14:12.152
I don't want socks.

248
00:14:12.153 --> 00:14:14.110
Why?
You'll get blisters.

249
00:14:14.111 --> 00:14:15.547
I just don't.

250
00:14:16.418 --> 00:14:18.375
Okay.

251
00:14:19.769 --> 00:14:21.162
Oh. Oh, wait. Dad!

252
00:14:22.946 --> 00:14:25.165
- Hey, hey, Dad!
- Yeah!

253
00:14:25.166 --> 00:14:26.558
- Hey. Um...
- Hey.

254
00:14:28.082 --> 00:14:29.256
I forgot to ask you.

255
00:14:29.257 --> 00:14:30.823
Um, a boy named Moose asked

256
00:14:30.824 --> 00:14:33.042
if he can cut our lawn for five bucks.

257
00:14:33.043 --> 00:14:35.697
Moose? Well, tell him thanks,
but no, thanks.

258
00:14:35.698 --> 00:14:37.090
I just got a new power mower

259
00:14:37.091 --> 00:14:39.092
and I'm really excited for the grass to grow.

260
00:14:40.877 --> 00:14:42.791
- All right. Knock 'em dead today, all right, sweetie?
- Okay.

261
00:14:42.792 --> 00:14:44.446
- Okay.
- Bye.

262
00:14:46.404 --> 00:14:48.524
I just need to warn you
one more time about the socks.

263
00:15:13.475 --> 00:15:14.650
Oh, Margaret's here.

264
00:15:20.177 --> 00:15:23.614
Hello.
Good, I thought you'd forget.

265
00:15:23.615 --> 00:15:24.746
Guys, this is Margaret,

266
00:15:24.747 --> 00:15:26.182
the one I was telling you about.

267
00:15:26.183 --> 00:15:28.402
- Margaret, this is Janie.
- Hi, nice to meet you.

268
00:15:28.403 --> 00:15:30.447
- Yeah, you, too.
- And this is Gretchen.

269
00:15:30.448 --> 00:15:33.276
- So, you're the fourth.
- Yeah.

270
00:15:33.277 --> 00:15:35.365
Well, you're lucky we saved you a seat.

271
00:15:35.366 --> 00:15:37.891
Or else you'd be sitting
next to Norman Fisher.

272
00:15:40.632 --> 00:15:42.285
Ugh.

273
00:15:42.286 --> 00:15:44.724
Oh, my God.
Oh, my God, don't look.

274
00:15:45.812 --> 00:15:48.465
Philip Leroy just walked in.

275
00:15:48.466 --> 00:15:51.251
I was praying so hard he'd be in our class.

276
00:15:51.252 --> 00:15:52.514
Who's Philip Leroy?

277
00:15:53.341 --> 00:15:54.603
Take a guess.

278
00:16:03.133 --> 00:16:04.221
Is that our teacher?

279
00:16:05.309 --> 00:16:08.137
Her?
No.

280
00:16:08.138 --> 00:16:10.793
That's Laura Danker.
Stay away from her, okay?

281
00:16:11.663 --> 00:16:12.968
My brother says that

282
00:16:12.969 --> 00:16:15.188
she goes behind the A
with him and Moose

283
00:16:15.189 --> 00:16:17.495
and lets them feel her up.

284
00:16:24.502 --> 00:16:26.416
Good morning, class.

285
00:16:26.417 --> 00:16:27.896
First, let me introduce myself.

286
00:16:27.897 --> 00:16:30.420
I am Mr. Benedict.

287
00:16:30.421 --> 00:16:32.772
And I'm your new sixth grade teacher.

288
00:16:34.338 --> 00:16:35.861
Please complete the following sentences

289
00:16:35.862 --> 00:16:39.168
so we can get to know each
other a little better, yeah?

290
00:16:39.169 --> 00:16:42.738
Now, I'll begin, just to
start things off for you guys.

291
00:16:43.826 --> 00:16:45.218
I love that I'm finally

292
00:16:45.219 --> 00:16:47.395
getting to be a teacher
for the first time.

293
00:16:49.223 --> 00:16:50.224
I hate...

294
00:16:51.051 --> 00:16:52.399
feeling self-conscious

295
00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:53.792
trying not to feel self-conscious because

296
00:16:53.793 --> 00:16:56.359
then you only feel more self-conscious

297
00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:57.534
and then you're blabbing in front of

298
00:16:57.535 --> 00:16:58.884
a whole bunch of kids.
Um...

299
00:16:58.885 --> 00:17:01.670
I'm looking forward to the year with you all.

300
00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:04.151
Okay, uh,
your turn.

301
00:17:14.422 --> 00:17:15.553
Pass it on.

302
00:17:28.349 --> 00:17:30.394
Yes.
Okay.

303
00:17:37.532 --> 00:17:39.621
Can any of you go in here?

304
00:17:42.711 --> 00:17:43.973
Ugh, no.

305
00:17:45.192 --> 00:17:46.802
Back in the box.

306
00:18:00.947 --> 00:18:04.558
Okay. All right. Enough.

307
00:18:04.559 --> 00:18:06.343
Enough, enough, enough.

308
00:18:19.791 --> 00:18:21.488
- Hello?
- Guess who?

309
00:18:21.489 --> 00:18:23.752
Oh. Sylvia, hi.
Um...

310
00:18:24.971 --> 00:18:27.495
- Margaret's not home yet.
- <i>It's 3:32.</i>

311
00:18:27.974 --> 00:18:29.496
<i>Yeah?</i>

312
00:18:29.497 --> 00:18:32.629
You said she's out at 3:15
and the walk is ten minutes.

313
00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:34.414
Yes, I did say that.
But, well...

314
00:18:34.415 --> 00:18:35.719
I'm sure she'll be

315
00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:37.360
walking through that door any minute now.

316
00:18:37.766 --> 00:18:39.071
Well...

317
00:18:39.072 --> 00:18:41.813
Okay.
I guess I'll just wait.

318
00:18:42.771 --> 00:18:43.815
Okay.

319
00:18:46.949 --> 00:18:48.689
So, how are you?

320
00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:52.171
I am fine.
I'm good. Yes.

321
00:18:52.172 --> 00:18:54.390
- And how are you?
- <i>Oh, fine.</i>

322
00:18:54.391 --> 00:18:56.827
I read that when you don't
have any loved ones around

323
00:18:56.828 --> 00:18:59.308
your life expectancy drops drastically,

324
00:18:59.309 --> 00:19:00.875
but, you know,
I've had a good run.

325
00:19:02.573 --> 00:19:05.836
You have.
You really have. Um...

326
00:19:05.837 --> 00:19:07.970
Margaret is here.
Just a second.

327
00:19:09.232 --> 00:19:11.191
- It's Grandma.
- Oh. Where's the Band-Aids?

328
00:19:11.974 --> 00:19:13.540
Mmm.

329
00:19:13.541 --> 00:19:15.281
- Grandma!
- <i>Honey!</i>

330
00:19:15.282 --> 00:19:17.631
How's New Jersey?
Are you okay?

331
00:19:17.632 --> 00:19:19.546
You can tell me the truth.

332
00:19:19.547 --> 00:19:21.027
You know, it's actually not that bad.

333
00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:25.987
Well, that's great news!
Wonderful news.

334
00:19:25.988 --> 00:19:27.597
Anyway, I was thinking

335
00:19:27.598 --> 00:19:30.557
that you could come visit
the weekend after next.

336
00:19:30.558 --> 00:19:32.080
<i>I'll get tickets to a show.</i>

337
00:19:32.081 --> 00:19:33.560
You can stay overnight,

338
00:19:33.561 --> 00:19:35.344
we'll have a little slumber party.

339
00:19:35.345 --> 00:19:36.606
That could be fun, right?

340
00:19:36.607 --> 00:19:38.130
Oh, I'd love that.

341
00:19:38.131 --> 00:19:40.567
Oh, I knew you would.
Great.

342
00:19:40.568 --> 00:19:42.438
And I'll tell your mother
it was your idea.

343
00:19:42.439 --> 00:19:44.179
- Okay?
- <i>Okay.</i>

344
00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:47.139
- Bye. Bye.
- <i>Bye, sweetheart.</i>

345
00:19:47.140 --> 00:19:48.532
- Bye.
<i>- Love you.</i>

346
00:19:52.754 --> 00:19:54.885
Hey, Mom, can I go Nancy's?

347
00:19:54.886 --> 00:19:56.887
Right now?
But you just got home.

348
00:19:56.888 --> 00:19:58.280
I haven't even heard about your day yet.

349
00:19:58.281 --> 00:20:01.153
- I know, but can I go?
- Can I have one word?

350
00:20:01.154 --> 00:20:03.155
Ugh... Uh?

351
00:20:03.156 --> 00:20:04.286
Is that a word?

352
00:20:04.287 --> 00:20:07.115
- Can I go? Bye.
- Yes, yes, okay, go.

353
00:20:07.116 --> 00:20:09.291
- I love you. Bye!
- Bye!

354
00:20:09.292 --> 00:20:12.251
Freddy was like,
"Boom, boom, look at me!"

355
00:20:12.252 --> 00:20:13.861
He's like,
"Make up your mind!"

356
00:20:13.862 --> 00:20:15.471
- She wants attention.
- Obviously.

357
00:20:15.472 --> 00:20:17.430
I know.
With her "boobala joobeelee."

358
00:20:17.431 --> 00:20:19.432
Hi!

359
00:20:19.433 --> 00:20:21.390
We were talking about Laura Danker again.

360
00:20:21.391 --> 00:20:24.567
Yeah. And how she got
even bigger over the summer.

361
00:20:24.568 --> 00:20:27.048
Yeah, she looked so grown up.

362
00:20:27.049 --> 00:20:28.963
You know she's worn
a bra since fourth grade?

363
00:20:28.964 --> 00:20:30.834
And I bet you a dollar
she gets her period, too.

364
00:20:30.835 --> 00:20:32.706
Well, I know for sure
someone in the school does.

365
00:20:32.707 --> 00:20:35.056
- How?
- I always check the bins.

366
00:20:35.057 --> 00:20:36.927
- You know those little bins in the stall?
- Mmm.

367
00:20:36.928 --> 00:20:39.322
All right. Let's get down to business, huh?

368
00:20:40.410 --> 00:20:41.628
- First of all...
- Thanks.

369
00:20:41.629 --> 00:20:43.760
...this secret club is a secret.

370
00:20:43.761 --> 00:20:46.589
Nobody tells anybody what happens here,

371
00:20:46.590 --> 00:20:47.982
- all right?
- Duh.

372
00:20:47.983 --> 00:20:49.984
Second, if you want
to be in the club,

373
00:20:49.985 --> 00:20:51.855
then you have to follow the rules.

374
00:20:51.856 --> 00:20:53.335
What kind of rules?

375
00:20:53.336 --> 00:20:56.035
Well, I don't know.
I'm thinking of them.

376
00:20:57.253 --> 00:20:59.429
Don't rush me.
Hmm.

377
00:21:00.517 --> 00:21:02.170
Oh, I have one.

378
00:21:02.171 --> 00:21:06.175
If you want to be in the club,
then you have to wear a bra.

379
00:21:07.872 --> 00:21:09.525
I have one.

380
00:21:09.526 --> 00:21:12.833
If you guys get your period,
you have to tell us about it.

381
00:21:12.834 --> 00:21:14.226
- Yes.
- Immediately.

382
00:21:14.227 --> 00:21:15.879
Every detail.
Especially how it feels.

383
00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:17.968
- Mmm-hmm.
- Ooh, mine is,

384
00:21:17.969 --> 00:21:19.405
we can make a Boy Book

385
00:21:19.406 --> 00:21:21.015
and write down the names
of the boys that we like.

386
00:21:21.016 --> 00:21:23.539
Mmm-hmm!
What about you, Margaret?

387
00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:24.889
What's your rule?

388
00:21:30.025 --> 00:21:31.373
Um...

389
00:21:31.374 --> 00:21:35.856
Yeah, with the Boy Books,
we have to show them

390
00:21:35.857 --> 00:21:39.904
to each other at every meeting
and we can't ever lie.

391
00:21:41.689 --> 00:21:43.603
All right.

392
00:21:43.604 --> 00:21:45.953
Let's get this party rolling.

393
00:21:47.042 --> 00:21:48.261
Whoo!

394
00:22:25.776 --> 00:22:27.169
Okay, honey.

395
00:22:30.825 --> 00:22:32.652
All right. Mmm.

396
00:22:32.653 --> 00:22:33.741
See you tomorrow.

397
00:22:35.873 --> 00:22:37.136
I want to get a bra.

398
00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:41.531
Oh.

399
00:22:43.316 --> 00:22:44.926
You... You think you need one?

400
00:22:45.970 --> 00:22:47.623
Oh, no.
Oh, honey.

401
00:22:47.624 --> 00:22:51.497
I'm so sorry.
No, I just mean that, uh...

402
00:22:51.498 --> 00:22:52.933
Bras are kind of a pain,

403
00:22:52.934 --> 00:22:55.327
so you know, why start sooner

404
00:22:55.328 --> 00:22:56.677
than you need to?

405
00:22:58.461 --> 00:23:01.246
But if you want one,
we... we can get you one.

406
00:23:01.247 --> 00:23:02.248
Well, yeah.

407
00:23:03.074 --> 00:23:04.162
So you want one?

408
00:23:04.163 --> 00:23:05.293
Yes.
I already said that.

409
00:23:05.294 --> 00:23:08.166
Right.
Okay.

410
00:23:08.167 --> 00:23:12.170
Great. Well, all right.
Well, then, we will do that.

411
00:23:12.171 --> 00:23:15.173
- This week?
- Yes. Good night.

412
00:23:15.174 --> 00:23:19.829
Good night. Good night,
my sweet. Okay.

413
00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:21.570
<i>So glad that's over with, God.</i>

414
00:23:31.059 --> 00:23:32.659
I'm sorry.
Hold on, just a moment.

415
00:23:34.062 --> 00:23:35.584
Are you here for the PTA meeting?

416
00:23:35.585 --> 00:23:39.066
Oh, yes. Hi, hi.
I'm Barbara Simon.

417
00:23:39.067 --> 00:23:42.722
Oh, Barbara! I'm Jan Wheeler.
Nancy's mother.

418
00:23:42.723 --> 00:23:45.159
- I met Margaret.
- Oh, oh.

419
00:23:45.160 --> 00:23:46.900
We're just about to get started,
so please come in.

420
00:23:46.901 --> 00:23:48.728
- Have a seat.
- Okay, thank you.

421
00:23:48.729 --> 00:23:50.077
- All right.
- Just anywhere is fine?

422
00:23:50.078 --> 00:23:51.513
- Here. Just right here.
- Okay, okay.

423
00:23:51.514 --> 00:23:53.516
Here we go.

424
00:23:55.126 --> 00:23:57.780
Thank you all for coming.

425
00:23:57.781 --> 00:24:00.435
Delano is nothing without
its dedicated parents.

426
00:24:00.436 --> 00:24:01.915
Let's dive right in and get started

427
00:24:01.916 --> 00:24:03.525
the way we do every year,

428
00:24:03.526 --> 00:24:05.527
by forming our committees.

429
00:24:05.528 --> 00:24:08.443
First up, we have the
Campus Improvement Committee.

430
00:24:08.444 --> 00:24:09.531
Any volunteers?

431
00:24:09.532 --> 00:24:11.229
Ooh.
Okay.

432
00:24:11.230 --> 00:24:13.535
Oh.
Wonderful.

433
00:24:13.536 --> 00:24:17.104
Uh-huh.
Barbara, I got you. Okay.

434
00:24:17.105 --> 00:24:20.282
Next, the Delano Social Committee.

435
00:24:20.935 --> 00:24:22.022
Sure, yeah.
Okay.

436
00:24:22.023 --> 00:24:25.417
- Okay.
- Great.

437
00:24:25.418 --> 00:24:27.550
All right.
The Fundraising Committee.

438
00:24:30.161 --> 00:24:31.336
Good for you, Barbara.

439
00:24:31.337 --> 00:24:32.815
This is going to be great.

440
00:24:32.816 --> 00:24:34.991
All right, pencils down.

441
00:24:34.992 --> 00:24:37.516
Kindly pass your worksheets forward.

442
00:24:37.517 --> 00:24:39.431
How'd you do, Margaret?

443
00:24:39.432 --> 00:24:40.519
I think I did pretty good.

444
00:24:40.520 --> 00:24:41.781
All right, uh...

445
00:24:41.782 --> 00:24:44.305
Before the bell,
I want to share some news

446
00:24:44.306 --> 00:24:46.873
that I think will make you all very happy.

447
00:24:46.874 --> 00:24:49.919
Now that you all
are in the sixth grade,

448
00:24:49.920 --> 00:24:54.054
you'll get to do a full,
year-long research project.

449
00:24:54.055 --> 00:24:55.795
Yes!

450
00:24:55.796 --> 00:24:57.275
The worst.

451
00:24:59.582 --> 00:25:00.756
Margaret, I would like to talk to you

452
00:25:00.757 --> 00:25:02.758
for a moment after class.

453
00:25:02.759 --> 00:25:05.240
Uh-oh.
What'd you do, Margaret?

454
00:25:11.159 --> 00:25:13.161
- Hi.
- Please have a seat.

455
00:25:15.598 --> 00:25:17.686
So basically,
I'm just having little chats

456
00:25:17.687 --> 00:25:19.949
with each student in advance
of your research projects

457
00:25:19.950 --> 00:25:21.386
to answer any questions

458
00:25:21.387 --> 00:25:23.519
or perhaps guide you toward a topic of choice.

459
00:25:24.390 --> 00:25:25.607
Oh.

460
00:25:25.608 --> 00:25:28.175
And I read your getting-to-know-you paper.

461
00:25:28.176 --> 00:25:30.220
And I noticed under the "I hate" section,

462
00:25:30.221 --> 00:25:33.049
you wrote
"religious holidays."

463
00:25:33.050 --> 00:25:35.836
Which I... I found curious.

464
00:25:39.143 --> 00:25:41.884
If you don't want to share,
you don't...

465
00:25:41.885 --> 00:25:43.059
You don't have to, Margaret.

466
00:25:43.060 --> 00:25:45.410
Oh, no.
It's just, um...

467
00:25:45.411 --> 00:25:47.325
I guess I just don't like those holidays

468
00:25:47.326 --> 00:25:49.327
because I don't celebrate any of them.

469
00:25:49.328 --> 00:25:51.590
My dad is Jewish and my mom's Christian,

470
00:25:51.591 --> 00:25:54.506
so instead of picking
which religion I am, uh,

471
00:25:54.507 --> 00:25:56.421
they just decided that I wouldn't have one

472
00:25:56.422 --> 00:25:58.597
and I can choose when I grow up.

473
00:25:58.598 --> 00:26:01.817
And have you given that much thought?

474
00:26:01.818 --> 00:26:03.993
Not really.
My grandma wants me to be Jewish.

475
00:26:03.994 --> 00:26:05.168
And your other grandparents

476
00:26:05.169 --> 00:26:07.432
want you to be Christian, I imagine.

477
00:26:07.433 --> 00:26:09.042
I don't know.
I've never met them before.

478
00:26:09.043 --> 00:26:10.739
They live in Ohio.

479
00:26:10.740 --> 00:26:12.263
So you've never met them at all?

480
00:26:14.396 --> 00:26:15.571
- No.
- Oh.

481
00:26:16.659 --> 00:26:19.923
Well, if I may suggest it,

482
00:26:21.011 --> 00:26:23.012
I feel like "religion" could be

483
00:26:23.013 --> 00:26:25.146
a very compelling research topic for you.

484
00:26:28.932 --> 00:26:30.193
<i>Tickets are tenth row,</i>

485
00:26:30.194 --> 00:26:32.805
<i>dead center, very hard to get.</i>

486
00:26:32.806 --> 00:26:34.763
- Tell her that.
<i>- I will.</i>

487
00:26:34.764 --> 00:26:36.983
- Is she excited?
- She's excited.

488
00:26:36.984 --> 00:26:39.987
Well, I mean, is she excited
or is she just excited?

489
00:26:40.553 --> 00:26:42.162
She's excited.

490
00:26:42.163 --> 00:26:44.730
Okay, okay, okay, okay, I'll let you go.
Well, I'm excited!

491
00:26:44.731 --> 00:26:46.515
- Okay, bye.
- <i>Bye.</i>

492
00:26:47.864 --> 00:26:48.951
Hey.

493
00:26:48.952 --> 00:26:50.562
- Hey.
- What happened to the couch?

494
00:26:50.563 --> 00:26:53.608
Uh, it's time to turn over a new leaf.

495
00:26:53.609 --> 00:26:56.132
I was thinking maybe something modern?

496
00:26:56.133 --> 00:26:58.570
I don't know. I have to think about it.
How was school?

497
00:26:58.571 --> 00:27:00.963
You're home a little later than usual, huh?

498
00:27:00.964 --> 00:27:02.835
Yeah.

499
00:27:02.836 --> 00:27:05.839
Hey.
How come I've never met your mom or dad?

500
00:27:06.796 --> 00:27:08.710
Um...

501
00:27:08.711 --> 00:27:10.538
Well, what made you think about that?

502
00:27:10.539 --> 00:27:12.279
Just wondering.

503
00:27:12.280 --> 00:27:14.890
I mean, I know that we don't see them

504
00:27:14.891 --> 00:27:16.718
because they're so far away,

505
00:27:16.719 --> 00:27:18.417
but why don't we even talk to them?

506
00:27:20.854 --> 00:27:23.029
We just, we just don't.

507
00:27:23.030 --> 00:27:25.119
It's, uh... It's, um...

508
00:27:26.250 --> 00:27:27.860
It's such a long story.

509
00:27:27.861 --> 00:27:29.296
What do you mean?

510
00:27:29.297 --> 00:27:31.951
I mean, I'll tell you another time.

511
00:27:31.952 --> 00:27:33.606
Why can't you just tell me now?

512
00:27:37.131 --> 00:27:38.132
Um...

513
00:27:43.659 --> 00:27:45.487
