00:58:19.928 --> 00:58:21.756
- Oh, I'll go.
- Okay.

1021
00:58:24.106 --> 00:58:25.107
I got it.

1022
00:58:26.065 --> 00:58:27.109
Got what?

1023
00:58:28.023 --> 00:58:29.460
My period.

1024
00:58:32.158 --> 00:58:34.246
I just don't really understand
how you got it first

1025
00:58:34.247 --> 00:58:35.639
when I have way more than you.

1026
00:58:35.640 --> 00:58:37.205
Well, that doesn't mean anything.

1027
00:58:37.206 --> 00:58:38.729
- Yes, it does, Gretchen.
- Okay, just tell us

1028
00:58:38.730 --> 00:58:41.036
- how it happened.
- Start from the very beginning.

1029
00:58:42.734 --> 00:58:46.563
Well, I was sitting there at dinner

1030
00:58:46.564 --> 00:58:48.173
eating my meatloaf

1031
00:58:48.174 --> 00:58:50.437
and I felt something coming out of me.

1032
00:58:51.264 --> 00:58:53.047
So I went to the bathroom,

1033
00:58:53.048 --> 00:58:56.748
pulled down my pants and
that's when I saw the blood.

1034
00:58:58.706 --> 00:59:00.141
So I called my mom

1035
00:59:00.142 --> 00:59:01.491
and I showed her.

1036
00:59:01.492 --> 00:59:03.536
And
she got some

1037
00:59:03.537 --> 00:59:06.365
"sanitary napkins,"
as she calls them.

1038
00:59:06.366 --> 00:59:08.150
I put one on and...

1039
00:59:09.891 --> 00:59:11.632
Well, that's the whole thing.

1040
00:59:14.069 --> 00:59:16.680
That's the whole thing?
Just that?

1041
00:59:16.681 --> 00:59:18.290
- I told you everything.
- No.

1042
00:59:18.291 --> 00:59:20.466
There has to be something more.

1043
00:59:20.467 --> 00:59:22.860
My sister said that it kinda has a smell.

1044
00:59:22.861 --> 00:59:24.731
But I haven't noticed that yet.

1045
00:59:24.732 --> 00:59:26.646
A smell?
Like what?

1046
00:59:26.647 --> 00:59:29.214
She said it kinda smells
like the monkey bars.

1047
00:59:29.215 --> 00:59:31.869
- The monkey bars? Ugh.
- Yeah.

1048
00:59:31.870 --> 00:59:34.088
I used to love the monkey bars.

1049
00:59:34.089 --> 00:59:38.179
But do you feel older now?
Like more mature?

1050
00:59:38.180 --> 00:59:39.659
Oh, yeah.

1051
00:59:39.660 --> 00:59:41.618
I don't know how to explain it

1052
00:59:41.619 --> 00:59:43.576
and you won't understand it till you get it,

1053
00:59:43.577 --> 00:59:46.710
but I feel like everything's changed.

1054
00:59:46.711 --> 00:59:47.972
Are you there, God?
It's me, Margaret.

1055
00:59:47.973 --> 00:59:49.495
I've never been so jealous my entire life

1056
00:59:49.496 --> 00:59:50.714
and I hate myself for being jealous.

1057
00:59:50.715 --> 00:59:53.020
Just please, please just let me grow

1058
00:59:53.021 --> 00:59:54.544
and let me get my period.

1059
00:59:54.545 --> 00:59:56.328
Let me just be normal
and regular like everybody else.

1060
00:59:56.329 --> 00:59:57.503
Just please, please,

1061
00:59:57.504 --> 00:59:59.064
please, please, please, please, please!

1062
01:00:02.117 --> 01:00:03.727
Amen.

1063
01:00:05.207 --> 01:00:07.513
I don't know if I want to do this.

1064
01:00:07.514 --> 01:00:09.864
It's fine.
It's just so that we're ready.

1065
01:00:10.648 --> 01:00:11.910
Just in case.

1066
01:00:19.265 --> 01:00:20.266
Come on.

1067
01:00:21.354 --> 01:00:22.529
Okay.

1068
01:00:27.012 --> 01:00:28.709
Next in line, please.

1069
01:00:29.580 --> 01:00:30.929
Please, God, let it be a lady.

1070
01:00:32.365 --> 01:00:33.453
Please.

1071
01:00:34.193 --> 01:00:35.933
Thank you.

1072
01:00:39.241 --> 01:00:41.242
- Hey, there.
- Hey.

1073
01:00:41.243 --> 01:00:42.809
- No...
- Let's just put them back.

1074
01:00:42.810 --> 01:00:45.247
No, come on.
Come on.

1075
01:01:17.584 --> 01:01:18.716
- Oh, my God!
- Oh!

1076
01:01:23.547 --> 01:01:26.158
The Tic Tacs!

1077
01:01:27.725 --> 01:01:29.726
- Why the Tic Tacs?
- I don't know.

1078
01:01:29.727 --> 01:01:32.120
- Everything worked out.
- Oh, man.

1079
01:02:17.426 --> 01:02:19.864
Uh, come in.

1080
01:02:23.128 --> 01:02:24.215
- Hi.
- Hey.

1081
01:02:24.216 --> 01:02:26.217
Uh, you've got a postcard.

1082
01:02:26.218 --> 01:02:29.350
- Oh. Thanks.
- Who's in D.C.?

1083
01:02:29.351 --> 01:02:33.312
Uh, Nancy.
Uh, they went for President's Day.

1084
01:02:34.095 --> 01:02:35.443
- Oh.
- Yeah.

1085
01:02:35.444 --> 01:02:37.402
Okay.

1086
01:02:37.403 --> 01:02:39.710
- You want the door closed?
- Yeah. Sure.

1087
01:02:45.672 --> 01:02:46.804
"I got it"?

1088
01:02:50.677 --> 01:02:52.418
Oh, come on!

1089
01:03:04.082 --> 01:03:08.041
Hello? Simon residence.
Sylvia speaking.

1090
01:03:08.042 --> 01:03:09.202
<i>Grandma?</i>

1091
01:03:09.914 --> 01:03:12.569
Margaret?
What's wrong?

1092
01:03:13.482 --> 01:03:14.875
I just really miss you.

1093
01:03:15.354 --> 01:03:16.355
<i>Oh, honey.</i>

1094
01:03:16.747 --> 01:03:18.269
Me, too.

1095
01:03:18.270 --> 01:03:20.663
<i>I'll be back next week
to see the Rockettes and...</i>

1096
01:03:20.664 --> 01:03:22.708
maybe could I come down

1097
01:03:22.709 --> 01:03:24.710
and stay the night like we did last time?

1098
01:03:24.711 --> 01:03:26.407
<i>Oh, sweetheart.</i>

1099
01:03:26.408 --> 01:03:28.846
I'd love to, I'd love...
But I...

1100
01:03:29.455 --> 01:03:30.456
<i>Well...</i>

1101
01:03:33.546 --> 01:03:35.634
I'm going to be in Florida then.

1102
01:03:35.635 --> 01:03:38.463
<i>I, uh, I heard about this hotel</i>

1103
01:03:38.464 --> 01:03:41.901
and there's a lot of people
my age there and, uh...

1104
01:03:41.902 --> 01:03:44.295
Um, okay.

1105
01:03:44.296 --> 01:03:46.559
Wait a minute. Wait.
Um...

1106
01:03:47.734 --> 01:03:50.040
What if you fly down to Florida

1107
01:03:50.041 --> 01:03:51.824
and spend a few days with me?

1108
01:03:51.825 --> 01:03:54.958
- <i>Isn't your spring break soon?</i>
- Yeah. The end of April.

1109
01:03:54.959 --> 01:03:57.047
Perfect!
I'll still be there.

1110
01:03:57.048 --> 01:03:58.396
I'll ask Mom and Dad.

1111
01:03:58.397 --> 01:04:00.267
Oh, great!

1112
01:04:00.268 --> 01:04:02.706
<i>That's my girl.
Bye, darling.</i>

1113
01:04:08.494 --> 01:04:10.190
Come on, come on!
Front row tickets!

1114
01:04:10.191 --> 01:04:13.585
- Front row tickets, remember?
- I'm coming! Yes, coming!

1115
01:04:14.718 --> 01:04:15.849
I'm so excited.

1116
01:04:18.809 --> 01:04:19.809
Hi.

1117
01:04:20.506 --> 01:04:21.638
- Hi.
- Hey.

1118
01:04:46.140 --> 01:04:48.360
- Excuse me.
- Okay.

1119
01:04:48.795 --> 01:04:49.795
Thank you.

1120
01:05:03.984 --> 01:05:05.115
Sorry.
Lefty.

1121
01:05:05.116 --> 01:05:06.508
Oh, no, it's okay.

1122
01:05:09.816 --> 01:05:11.338
Do you know if the waiter's anywhere?

1123
01:05:11.339 --> 01:05:14.255
Oh. You can have mine.
I didn't drink any out of it.

1124
01:05:14.821 --> 01:05:15.821
Thanks.

1125
01:05:17.345 --> 01:05:18.346
Hey.

1126
01:05:20.827 --> 01:05:22.001
Do you know something

1127
01:05:22.002 --> 01:05:23.655
I've always liked about you, Margaret?

1128
01:05:23.656 --> 01:05:25.091
- No?
- Come with me.

1129
01:05:25.092 --> 01:05:26.571
I got to go to the bathroom.

1130
01:05:26.572 --> 01:05:28.400
We'll be right back.
Don't touch my food.

1131
01:05:31.403 --> 01:05:33.163
You know, I've had to go
since we got here...

1132
01:05:34.580 --> 01:05:36.320
...and then I drank, like,
three 7Ups or something.

1133
01:05:36.321 --> 01:05:37.930
Uh-huh.

1134
01:05:41.674 --> 01:05:42.719
Oh, no.

1135
01:05:43.763 --> 01:05:44.895
- Oh, no.
- What?

1136
01:05:45.591 --> 01:05:47.158
Oh, please.
Oh, no.

1137
01:05:48.637 --> 01:05:49.682
Nancy?

1138
01:05:51.292 --> 01:05:52.771
Oh, no.

1139
01:05:52.772 --> 01:05:54.033
Nancy, what's wrong?

1140
01:05:54.034 --> 01:05:55.252
Go get my mom, Margaret.

1141
01:05:55.253 --> 01:05:56.906
- What's going on?
- Go get my mom.

1142
01:05:56.907 --> 01:05:58.777
- Please, quick.
- Let me in.

1143
01:05:58.778 --> 01:06:02.085
Please, please just go get my mom!

1144
01:06:02.086 --> 01:06:03.740
Okay, okay, I'll be right back.

1145
01:06:06.960 --> 01:06:10.223
Mrs. Wheeler, Nancy's crying.
She needs you.

1146
01:06:10.224 --> 01:06:12.270
Oh, oh.
All right.

1147
01:06:18.102 --> 01:06:19.189
Nancy?

1148
01:06:19.190 --> 01:06:21.931
- Nancy?
- Oh, Mom, please help me.

1149
01:06:21.932 --> 01:06:24.020
- Please help me. Please.
- The door's locked, Nancy.

1150
01:06:24.021 --> 01:06:25.543
I can't get in.
You have to unlock it.

1151
01:06:25.544 --> 01:06:28.198
- I can't open it, I can't.
- Yes, you can, Nancy.

1152
01:06:28.199 --> 01:06:30.201
Unlock this door. Come on.

1153
01:06:31.855 --> 01:06:32.856
Let me in.

1154
01:06:39.906 --> 01:06:40.950
What's going on?

1155
01:06:42.648 --> 01:06:44.692
All right, all right, calm down.

1156
01:06:44.693 --> 01:06:46.346
Calm down, I can't help you.

1157
01:06:46.347 --> 01:06:48.914
Hmm? Hey, look at me.
Calm down.

1158
01:06:48.915 --> 01:06:51.657
I can't help you if you don't
stop crying and talk to me.

1159
01:06:55.313 --> 01:06:57.489
Hey.
What is it?

1160
01:07:05.714 --> 01:07:09.327
Oh. Well, all right.
Um...

1161
01:07:11.155 --> 01:07:12.504
Here.
We'll just, uh...

1162
01:07:14.375 --> 01:07:15.767
Margaret?

1163
01:07:15.768 --> 01:07:17.247
Margaret.

1164
01:07:17.248 --> 01:07:21.077
Would you get Nancy a pad, please

1165
01:07:21.078 --> 01:07:23.384
from the dispenser on the wall?

1166
01:07:25.212 --> 01:07:27.518
She got her period, sweetie.

1167
01:07:27.519 --> 01:07:29.868
Does she always act like that?

1168
01:07:29.869 --> 01:07:32.959
Well, it's her first time.
She's just a little scared.

1169
01:07:46.799 --> 01:07:47.844
Thank you, sweetie.

1170
01:07:49.323 --> 01:07:50.585
All right.
Yeah?

1171
01:07:52.718 --> 01:07:53.806
All right.

1172
01:07:55.590 --> 01:07:57.548
Well, you girls wash up.

1173
01:07:57.549 --> 01:07:59.856
I'm going to go tell the others not to worry.

1174
01:08:03.381 --> 01:08:06.036
Not too long now.
Okay?

1175
01:08:37.284 --> 01:08:40.374
<i>Are you there, God?
It's me, Margaret.</i>

1176
01:08:42.159 --> 01:08:43.900
<i>I don't even know what to say.</i>

1177
01:09:05.008 --> 01:09:06.574
I'm going to Florida?

1178
01:09:07.706 --> 01:09:09.882
- Happy birthday.
- Mom. Thank you so much.

1179
01:09:15.279 --> 01:09:16.280
Hey!

1180
01:09:17.716 --> 01:09:19.804
- Happy birthday.
- Thank you.

1181
01:09:19.805 --> 01:09:21.458
Why do we have different seats?

1182
01:09:21.459 --> 01:09:23.591
He said we're in groups
to study different countries.

1183
01:09:49.530 --> 01:09:51.401
Oh. Hey.

1184
01:09:51.402 --> 01:09:53.881
Hey.
Happy birthday.

1185
01:09:53.882 --> 01:09:54.970
- Thanks.
- Oh, and, uh,

1186
01:09:54.971 --> 01:09:58.234
- I got you something.
- Ow!

1187
01:09:58.235 --> 01:10:00.062
It's a pinch to grow an inch.

1188
01:10:00.063 --> 01:10:03.283
And you know where you need that inch.
Hey.

1189
01:10:06.504 --> 01:10:08.984
<i>Are you there, God?
It's me, Margaret.</i>

1190
01:10:08.985 --> 01:10:12.248
<i>I hate Philip Leroy.
I hate him.</i>

1191
01:10:12.249 --> 01:10:15.381
<i>I hate Laura Danker, too!
With her big boobs.</i>

1192
01:10:15.382 --> 01:10:17.994
<i>"Ooh, look at me, everybody,
I'm wearing a sweater."</i>

1193
01:10:19.038 --> 01:10:21.735
<i>I hate Nancy.
That liar!</i>

1194
01:10:21.736 --> 01:10:23.389
<i>And Norman Fisher,
the way that he reads</i>

1195
01:10:23.390 --> 01:10:26.218
<i>with his stupid lips flapping everywhere!</i>

1196
01:10:26.219 --> 01:10:30.092
<i>Please. Please, just hurry up
and get me to Florida!</i>

1197
01:10:38.884 --> 01:10:40.232
Philip and Norman should be here.

1198
01:10:40.233 --> 01:10:42.713
They make us do all the work.

1199
01:10:42.714 --> 01:10:44.585
What time is your mom picking you up?

1200
01:10:45.499 --> 01:10:46.934
Not till later.

1201
01:10:46.935 --> 01:10:48.806
I have to go to St. Thomas
for Confession first.

1202
01:10:48.807 --> 01:10:51.678
Confession?

1203
01:10:51.679 --> 01:10:53.879
It's just something you have
to do when you're Catholic.

1204
01:10:54.465 --> 01:10:55.814
What do you confess?

1205
01:10:57.555 --> 01:10:58.556
Things.

1206
01:11:00.123 --> 01:11:02.212
What kinds of things?

1207
01:11:06.520 --> 01:11:07.521
Never mind.

1208
01:11:16.139 --> 01:11:18.139
You're just copying straight
out of the <i>World Book.</i>

1209
01:11:18.619 --> 01:11:20.446
It's four words.

1210
01:11:20.447 --> 01:11:22.840
"Germany invaded Belgium when..."

1211
01:11:22.841 --> 01:11:24.363
So, you're still cheating.

1212
01:11:24.364 --> 01:11:26.235
Mr. Benedict will know if you're cheating.

1213
01:11:26.236 --> 01:11:28.759
I'm not cheating!
Jeez!

1214
01:11:32.590 --> 01:11:33.894
Quit acting like you know everything

1215
01:11:33.895 --> 01:11:35.157
and you're so great.

1216
01:11:35.158 --> 01:11:36.810
This has nothing to do with being great.

1217
01:11:36.811 --> 01:11:38.639
I know all about the stuff that you do.

1218
01:11:40.337 --> 01:11:41.815
What's that supposed to mean?

1219
01:11:41.816 --> 01:11:43.383
I heard about you and Moose Freed.

1220
01:11:44.428 --> 01:11:46.298
What about me and Moose Freed?

1221
01:11:46.299 --> 01:11:48.996
Oh, how you and Evan and Moose
go behind the A

1222
01:11:48.997 --> 01:11:50.563
And why would I do that?

1223
01:11:50.564 --> 01:11:54.437
I don't know why you do it.
But I know why they do it.

1224
01:11:54.438 --> 01:11:56.439
So they can feel you up
or something and you let them.

1225
01:11:56.440 --> 01:11:57.657
You're a liar.
You're lying!

1226
01:11:57.658 --> 01:11:58.745
I'm not lying.

1227
01:11:58.746 --> 01:12:00.225
You're just like Nancy.

1228
01:12:00.226 --> 01:12:03.054
All you do is pick on people
and make up stories.

1229
01:12:03.055 --> 01:12:05.015
You think I don't know
about you and your friends?

1230
01:12:17.417 --> 01:12:18.809
Laura!

1231
01:12:18.810 --> 01:12:21.594
Wait. Please! Laura!

1232
01:12:21.595 --> 01:12:24.119
- Wait up. Please!
- You think I don't know

1233
01:12:24.120 --> 01:12:26.208
that all of you make fun of me
like it's some kind of game?

1234
01:12:26.209 --> 01:12:27.513
- It's not me.
- Do you think I want to be

1235
01:12:27.514 --> 01:12:29.254
the biggest kid in the class?

1236
01:12:29.255 --> 01:12:32.301
How would you feel if you were
to wear a bra in fourth grade

1237
01:12:32.302 --> 01:12:33.389
and everybody called you names

1238
01:12:33.390 --> 01:12:35.000
just because of how you looked?

1239
01:12:36.088 --> 01:12:37.133
I don't know.

1240
01:12:41.789 --> 01:12:44.140
Hey, wait.
I really am sorry.

1241
01:13:02.767 --> 01:13:03.985
Laura?

1242
01:13:05.944 --> 01:13:06.988
Laura.

1243
01:13:24.049 --> 01:13:26.746
<i>I'm the worst person
who ever lived, God.</i>

1244
01:13:26.747 --> 01:13:29.359
<i>I picked on Laura Danker
just because I felt mean.</i>

1245
01:13:30.882 --> 01:13:33.710
<i>I don't want to be like Nancy.</i>

1246
01:13:33.711 --> 01:13:36.540
<i>I don't even know if I want to
be friends with her anymore.</i>

1247
01:13:39.369 --> 01:13:40.935
<i>I've been looking for you, God.</i>

1248
01:13:42.937 --> 01:13:45.112
<i>I looked for you in Temple,</i>

1249
01:13:45.113 --> 01:13:46.550
<i>I looked for you in Church...</i>

1250
01:13:48.247 --> 01:13:49.814
<i>I didn't feel you at all.</i>

1251
01:13:52.686 --> 01:13:54.210
<i>Why? Why, God?</i>

1252
01:13:56.037 --> 01:13:58.823
<i>Why do I only feel you when I'm alone?</i>

1253
01:14:03.219 --> 01:14:05.611
Yes, my child.

1254
01:14:05.612 --> 01:14:08.049
Do you have something you'd like to confess?

1255
01:14:10.008 --> 01:14:11.183
Um...

1256
01:14:17.407 --> 01:14:18.885
I...

1257
01:14:18.886 --> 01:14:20.932
I did something really awful.

1258
01:14:23.108 --> 01:14:24.240
And...

1259
01:14:26.807 --> 01:14:28.113
I'm really sorry.

1260
01:15:00.014 --> 01:15:01.798
<i>"Dear Barbara,</i>

1261
01:15:01.799 --> 01:15:04.104
"your letter felt like an answer to prayer.

1262
01:15:04.105 --> 01:15:06.455
"Your father and I have been
thinking about you a lot.

1263
01:15:06.456 --> 01:15:09.022
"We're getting older and suddenly,
more than anything,

1264
01:15:09.023 --> 01:15:12.983
"we'd like to see our only daughter

1265
01:15:12.984 --> 01:15:15.291
"and finally get to know our
granddaughter, Margaret Ann."

1266
01:15:17.336 --> 01:15:18.728
"We're flying east next week,

1267
01:15:18.729 --> 01:15:20.556
"and we sincerely hope you'll let us visit.

1268
01:15:20.557 --> 01:15:22.559
"Love, your mother, Mary Hutchins."

1269
01:15:29.522 --> 01:15:30.784
So you sent them a card?

1270
01:15:33.352 --> 01:15:34.788
I don't know why.

1271
01:15:44.537 --> 01:15:45.755
Do you remember what it was like

1272
01:15:45.756 --> 01:15:47.323
when they just cast you out?

1273
01:15:49.020 --> 01:15:50.107
Yes.

1274
01:15:50.108 --> 01:15:51.152
Do you?

1275
01:15:52.153 --> 01:15:53.719
Because I remember.

1276
01:15:53.720 --> 01:15:54.895
I know.
I know.

1277
01:15:55.983 --> 01:15:57.942
How they treated you was just...

1278
01:15:59.117 --> 01:16:00.466
- I know.
- How they treated me?

1279
01:16:01.598 --> 01:16:03.642
They think you're going to hell

1280
01:16:03.643 --> 01:16:05.036
because you married a Jew.

1281
01:16:06.124 --> 01:16:07.343
Think about that.

1282
01:16:07.908 --> 01:16:08.909
I...

1283
01:16:09.997 --> 01:16:11.433
I know.

1284
01:16:11.434 --> 01:16:14.480
Do you really, really want to
open up that door?

1285
01:16:15.307 --> 01:16:16.699
We have a good life.

1286
01:16:16.700 --> 01:16:17.962
Yes.
Yes.

1287
01:16:19.485 --> 01:16:20.485
I...

1288
01:16:21.879 --> 01:16:26.100
But what if this means...
they've changed?

1289
01:16:29.495 --> 01:16:30.496
And if they haven't?

1290
01:16:34.544 --> 01:16:36.110
They're my parents.

1291
01:16:38.809 --> 01:16:40.157
Mmm.

1292
01:16:40.158 --> 01:16:41.998
- The only ones I got.
- They are your parents.

1293
01:16:43.117 --> 01:16:45.249
Oh, God.

1294
01:16:45.250 --> 01:16:48.121
Oh, my goodness.

1295
01:16:48.122 --> 01:16:49.167
I'm sorry.

1296
01:16:52.823 --> 01:16:53.866
What's going on?

1297
01:16:53.867 --> 01:16:55.390
Um...

1298
01:16:55.391 --> 01:16:57.828
- Oh.
- Oh, honey, um...

1299
01:16:59.090 --> 01:17:00.265
Uh...

1300
01:17:02.136 --> 01:17:03.615
We got a letter

1301
01:17:03.616 --> 01:17:06.401
from, um, from my parents,
from your grandparents.

1302
01:17:06.402 --> 01:17:08.272
And they're coming to visit next week.

1303
01:17:08.273 --> 01:17:10.579
- Next... next week?
- Mmm-hmm.

1304
01:17:10.580 --> 01:17:12.363
They're really excited to meet you.

1305
01:17:12.364 --> 01:17:14.061
I won't be here.
I'll be in Florida.

1306
01:17:17.238 --> 01:17:19.152
I'm still going to Florida, aren't I?

1307
01:17:19.153 --> 01:17:21.981
- Margaret, look...
- No. What?

1308
01:17:21.982 --> 01:17:24.157
I can't even go to Florida now?

1309
01:17:24.158 --> 01:17:26.072
Come on, I don't even want to see them.

1310
01:17:26.073 --> 01:17:27.639
I want to see Grandma.

1311
01:17:27.640 --> 01:17:29.946
I know. I know and we will
make this up to you.

1312
01:17:29.947 --> 01:17:31.948
I promise, you will go to Florida,

1313
01:17:31.949 --> 01:17:34.211
- just another time.
- No, I don't want

1314
01:17:34.212 --> 01:17:35.822
to go to Florida another time.

1315
01:17:36.997 --> 01:17:38.563
Does Grandma know about this?

1316
01:17:38.564 --> 01:17:40.260
No, not yet.
We have to call her.

1317
01:17:40.261 --> 01:17:42.437
Well, I'm not doing it.
You can do it yourself.

1318
01:17:42.438 --> 01:17:44.308
- No, of course. Of course.
- Let me handle that.

1319
01:17:44.309 --> 01:17:46.311
- No, I will...
- Please let me call. Please.

1320
01:17:52.404 --> 01:17:54.797
To this beautiful day.

1321
01:17:57.627 --> 01:17:58.889
Just one moment.

1322
01:17:59.933 --> 01:18:01.543
Don't eat all the cheese without me.

1323
01:18:02.936 --> 01:18:05.372
I'm just kidding.
You eat as much as you want.

1324
01:18:05.373 --> 01:18:07.244
Depending on your cholesterol.

1325
01:18:07.245 --> 01:18:09.334
I'm sure it's low.

1326
01:18:14.861 --> 01:18:16.079
Simon residence.

1327
01:18:16.080 --> 01:18:17.689
<i>Hi, Mom. Yes. Uh...</i>

1328
01:18:17.690 --> 01:18:19.169
Herb?

1329
01:18:19.170 --> 01:18:20.823
Uh, Margaret's, uh, plan
to come to Florida next week

1330
01:18:20.824 --> 01:18:21.911
isn't going to work out.

1331
01:18:21.912 --> 01:18:22.913
I'm really sorry.

1332
01:18:24.218 --> 01:18:25.498
<i>Just give me the phone.</i>

1333
01:18:26.830 --> 01:18:27.960
<i>Hey, Grandma.</i>

1334
01:18:27.961 --> 01:18:30.006
Margaret, what happened?
What's going on?

1335
01:18:30.007 --> 01:18:32.225
We...

1336
01:18:32.226 --> 01:18:34.881
We got a letter that my
other grandparents are coming.

1337
01:18:36.100 --> 01:18:39.972
<i>And I just really wanted to see you.</i>

1338
01:18:39.973 --> 01:18:41.888
Put your mother on the phone right now.

1339
01:18:43.542 --> 01:18:45.239
- Oh, no...
- It's okay.

1340
01:18:47.807 --> 01:18:48.981
Sylvia.

1341
01:18:48.982 --> 01:18:50.635
What the hell is going on, Barbara?

1342
01:18:50.636 --> 01:18:53.682
Sylvia, I'm so very sorry about this

1343
01:18:53.683 --> 01:18:56.946
and I will try and explain it another time.

1344
01:18:56.947 --> 01:18:58.904
No. You're going to explain right now.

1345
01:18:58.905 --> 01:19:00.428
I'm sorry, I have to...
I have to go.

1346
01:19:05.216 --> 01:19:07.652
<i>Are you there, God?
It's me, Margaret.</i>

1347
01:19:07.653 --> 01:19:10.133
- <i>I'm absolutely miserable.</i>
- I am so sorry.

1348
01:19:10.134 --> 01:19:12.440
<i>Everything is going wrong.
Everything.</i>

1349
01:19:13.137 --> 01:19:14.790
<i>I'm begging you.</i>

1350
01:19:14.791 --> 01:19:17.880
<i>Make something happen
so that they don't come</i>

1351
01:19:17.881 --> 01:19:19.709
<i>and I can still go to Florida.</i>

1352
01:19:28.631 --> 01:19:30.196
Please, Margaret.
Even if it's fake,

1353
01:19:30.197 --> 01:19:32.373
can you just look happy?

1354
01:19:33.940 --> 01:19:35.898
Or at least not so unhappy?

1355
01:19:37.291 --> 01:19:39.379
Why do you even want to see them?

1356
01:19:39.380 --> 01:19:41.165
After everything that they did to you?

1357
01:19:43.384 --> 01:19:48.475
Because I want them to see
how great we've done.

1358
01:19:48.476 --> 01:19:51.567
I... And how proud I am of our family.

1359
01:19:56.615 --> 01:19:58.138
Hey! Hello.

1360
01:19:59.183 --> 01:20:00.227
That's them.

1361
01:20:00.924 --> 01:20:01.925
Okay.

1362
01:20:04.580 --> 01:20:05.581
Hi!

1363
01:20:07.060 --> 01:20:09.584
They might hug you,
I don't know.

1364
01:20:09.585 --> 01:20:10.847
Just be prepared.

1365
01:20:15.025 --> 01:20:16.286
- Hi!
- Hello!

1366
01:20:16.287 --> 01:20:18.375
Hello.
It's so nice to see you.

1367
01:20:18.376 --> 01:20:20.596
Oh, you too, Barbara.

1368
01:20:22.685 --> 01:20:23.773
Oh.

1369
01:20:29.213 --> 01:20:30.780
- Hi, honey.
- Oh.

1370
01:20:34.697 --> 01:20:36.786
- This must be Margaret Ann.
- Mmm-hmm.

1371
01:20:40.180 --> 01:20:41.920
We're very glad to meet you.

1372
01:20:41.921 --> 01:20:44.358
- Yes, we are. Yes, we are.
- Me, too.

1373
01:20:45.142 --> 01:20:46.230
Um...

1374
01:20:47.448 --> 01:20:49.711
Bags!
We'll get the bags.

1375
01:20:49.712 --> 01:20:53.149
Um, Herb is just out, uh,
with the car.

1376
01:20:53.150 --> 01:20:55.325
- Yeah, so... Okay.
- Okay.

1377
01:20:55.326 --> 01:20:57.457
Just out here to the right.

1378
01:20:57.458 --> 01:20:59.199
The blue car there.
Yep.

1379
01:21:01.201 --> 01:21:02.854
Hey.

1380
01:21:02.855 --> 01:21:04.595
- Youse okay? Yeah?
- Yeah.

1381
01:21:04.596 --> 01:21:06.249
Mom, Dad, you remember Herb?

1382
01:21:06.250 --> 01:21:07.511
- Yeah. Hello, Herb.
- Hi.

1383
01:21:07.512 --> 01:21:08.773
- How are you?
- Okay.

1384
01:21:08.774 --> 01:21:10.428
- Hi. Nice to see you.
- Hello.

1385
01:21:11.647 --> 01:21:12.995
Um, should I...
I'll take this for you.

1386
01:21:12.996 --> 01:21:14.084
Oh.

1387
01:21:17.609 --> 01:21:18.653
All right.

1388
01:21:18.654 --> 01:21:19.916
Okay.

1389
01:21:21.047 --> 01:21:22.134
All right.
Should I put these up?

1390
01:21:22.135 --> 01:21:23.441
Oh, yes.
Thank you.

1391
01:21:24.964 --> 01:21:28.663
Here we are.
Make yourselves comfortable.

1392
01:21:28.664 --> 01:21:30.577
- Lovely home.
- Yeah!

1393
01:21:30.578 --> 01:21:33.016
Thank you.
Yes. Uh...

1394
01:21:34.017 --> 01:21:35.713
Okay.
So, uh, Margaret, uh,

1395
01:21:35.714 --> 01:21:36.932
can you show them to their room?

1396
01:21:36.933 --> 01:21:39.630
And, um,
I'll just get dinner started.

1397
01:21:39.631 --> 01:21:42.460
Sure.
Um, up this way.

1398
01:21:46.507 --> 01:21:48.857
Gosh, you look just like your mom

1399
01:21:48.858 --> 01:21:50.467
when she was your age.

1400
01:21:50.468 --> 01:21:52.775
Um, yeah. This way.

1401
01:22:00.391 --> 01:22:02.740
- Hi.
- Hey.

1402
01:22:02.741 --> 01:22:04.002
How are you doing?

1403
01:22:04.003 --> 01:22:06.265
Uh... How are you doing?

1404
01:22:06.266 --> 01:22:08.311
Um, I used up all my small talk

1405
01:22:08.312 --> 01:22:09.529
- in the car.
- Oh, God.

1406
01:22:09.530 --> 01:22:11.707
Do they like sports?
TV shows?

1407
01:22:13.621 --> 01:22:15.710
Game shows.
They used to watch game shows.

1408
01:22:15.711 --> 01:22:18.800
Okay. Game shows, game shows.

1409
01:22:18.801 --> 01:22:20.105
Hmm.

1410
01:22:20.106 --> 01:22:21.629
Um, coming!

1411
01:22:24.415 --> 01:22:25.459
Herb!

1412
01:22:26.286 --> 01:22:27.417
Mom!

1413
01:22:27.418 --> 01:22:29.593
Baby!
Come give your mom a big hug.

1414
01:22:29.594 --> 01:22:30.899
Oh.

1415
01:22:30.900 --> 01:22:32.683
- Oh. Look at your little face.
- Sylvia?

1416
01:22:32.684 --> 01:22:34.119
Yeah.
My mom is here.

1417
01:22:34.120 --> 01:22:35.642
Uh, yes, she is.
What's happening?

1418
01:22:35.643 --> 01:22:37.644
Well, Margaret said she needed to see me,

1419
01:22:37.645 --> 01:22:39.037
so we flew out from Florida.

1420
01:22:39.038 --> 01:22:40.256
Are your parents here yet?

1421
01:22:40.257 --> 01:22:43.041
Oh. This is Morris Binamin.

1422
01:22:43.042 --> 01:22:45.130
Rhymes with cinnamon.

1423
01:22:45.131 --> 01:22:47.393
- Hi.
- Grandma!

1424
01:22:47.394 --> 01:22:50.309
There's my Margaret!
Oh!

1425
01:22:50.310 --> 01:22:52.311
- Did you know?
- I had no... I know.

1426
01:22:52.312 --> 01:22:53.617
I missed you so much!

1427
01:22:53.618 --> 01:22:54.966
I thought you were in Florida.

1428
01:22:54.967 --> 01:22:56.794
I know. Well,
Florida came to you.

1429
01:22:56.795 --> 01:22:58.230
Uh...

1430
01:22:58.231 --> 01:23:01.756
Mom, Dad, this is Sylvia.
Herb's mom.

1431
01:23:01.757 --> 01:23:05.672
Sylvia, this... These are
my parents, Paul and Mary.

1432
01:23:05.673 --> 01:23:07.370
Hello.

1433
01:23:07.371 --> 01:23:08.938
Hello.

1434
01:23:11.723 --> 01:23:12.810
We have pot roast.

1435
01:23:12.811 --> 01:23:14.333
Sure.

1436
01:23:17.207 --> 01:23:18.425
Mmm.

1437
01:23:19.731 --> 01:23:21.123
- Mmm.
- Oh, yeah.

1438
01:23:21.124 --> 01:23:23.386
- Dinner is delicious, Barbara.
- Oh, my God, yes.

1439
01:23:23.387 --> 01:23:26.171
- Oh.
- You have definitely improved.

1440
01:23:26.172 --> 01:23:28.261
- It is very nice.
- Thank you.

1441
01:23:30.437 --> 01:23:35.354
Well, I have to admit
it was a bit of a jolt, um,

1442
01:23:35.355 --> 01:23:39.358
but it's nice to have everyone here together.

1443
01:23:39.359 --> 01:23:40.883
The whole family.

1444
01:23:43.494 --> 01:23:45.843
And Mr. Binamin.

1445
01:23:45.844 --> 01:23:47.366
Nice to have you, too.

1446
01:23:50.370 --> 01:23:51.937
- <i>L'chaim.
- L'chaim.</i>

1447
01:23:53.809 --> 01:23:57.333
<i>L'chaim.
L'chaim.</i>

1448
01:23:57.334 --> 01:24:00.336
<i>L'chaim. L'chaim. L'chaim. L'chaim. L'chaim.</i>

1449
01:24:00.337 --> 01:24:02.252
To life!

1450
01:24:09.128 --> 01:24:10.564
So, um, do you watch <i>Jeopardy!?</i>

1451
01:24:15.831 --> 01:24:18.006
I used to braid your mama's hair

1452
01:24:18.007 --> 01:24:19.181
when she was a little girl.

1453
01:24:19.182 --> 01:24:21.096
Did your mom ever braid your hair?

1454
01:24:21.097 --> 01:24:23.794
Um, yeah, she used to do it all the time.

1455
01:24:23.795 --> 01:24:26.579
I can see she taught you how
to braid with your bracelet.

1456
01:24:26.580 --> 01:24:27.711
Yeah.

1457
01:24:27.712 --> 01:24:29.104
Oh, there's just so much

1458
01:24:29.105 --> 01:24:30.714
we want to get to know about you, Margaret.

1459
01:24:30.715 --> 01:24:32.455
Twelve years is a lot to catch up on.

1460
01:24:32.456 --> 01:24:33.718
Yeah.
A long time.

1461
01:24:34.632 --> 01:24:36.852
So, uh, we were wondering...

1462
01:24:38.636 --> 01:24:40.289
Do you go to Sunday school?

1463
01:24:40.290 --> 01:24:42.553
Or, uh, have you ever thought about it?

1464
01:24:43.728 --> 01:24:47.035
- Uh...
- Nope. Never. Not once.

1465
01:24:47.036 --> 01:24:49.559
We asked Margaret the question, Sylvia.

1466
01:24:49.560 --> 01:24:50.647
Margaret?

1467
01:24:50.648 --> 01:24:52.170
Well, you're wasting your time

1468
01:24:52.171 --> 01:24:55.086
because Margaret went
to Temple and she's Jewish.

1469
01:24:55.087 --> 01:24:56.827
What did you say?

1470
01:24:56.828 --> 01:24:57.915
Excuse me.

1471
01:24:57.916 --> 01:24:59.395
Margaret went to Temple.

1472
01:24:59.396 --> 01:25:01.049
- Okay, Mom, you're done.
- What are you talking about?

1473
01:25:01.050 --> 01:25:02.833
- Okay, that's it.
- Well, you left the room

1474
01:25:02.834 --> 01:25:04.661
and they're trying to convert her.

1475
01:25:04.662 --> 01:25:05.967
Well, Margaret has the right to be baptized

1476
01:25:05.968 --> 01:25:07.142
if she wants to be.

1477
01:25:07.143 --> 01:25:09.100
- Baptized?
- If she wants to be.

1478
01:25:09.101 --> 01:25:10.301
I can't believe this.

1479
01:25:11.625 --> 01:25:13.017
I can't believe you're doing this.

1480
01:25:13.018 --> 01:25:14.845
All right. Everyone,
this discussion is over.

1481
01:25:14.846 --> 01:25:16.847
We're her parents and this discussion is over.

1482
01:25:16.848 --> 01:25:18.936
Yeah, you're right, it's over,
because she's already Jewish.

1483
01:25:18.937 --> 01:25:20.633
- Sylvia!
- Well, in our eyes,

1484
01:25:20.634 --> 01:25:24.159
- she's Christian.
- No, no! Margaret is nothing!

1485
01:25:24.160 --> 01:25:27.249
Margaret is
not Jewish or Christian.

1486
01:25:27.250 --> 01:25:30.165
She is no religion until she decides.

1487
01:25:30.166 --> 01:25:31.340
Well, how can she be Jewish

1488
01:25:31.341 --> 01:25:33.037
- if her mother is Christian?
- Stop.

1489
01:25:33.038 --> 01:25:34.604
You were never there for her.
You abandoned her.

1490
01:25:34.605 --> 01:25:35.735
What does it matter?

1491
01:25:35.736 --> 01:25:37.215
Do you think that we wanted this?

1492
01:25:40.263 --> 01:25:41.351
Stop it!

1493
01:25:42.743 --> 01:25:44.440
All of you, just stop it.

1494
01:25:44.441 --> 01:25:47.269
I don't care.
I don't care anymore.

1495
01:25:47.270 --> 01:25:49.575
It's all just so stupid, religion!

1496
01:25:49.576 --> 01:25:50.925
Just stop fighting!

1497
01:25:50.926 --> 01:25:53.231
I... I don't want a religion.

1498
01:25:53.232 --> 01:25:55.495
- I don't care. I don't care!
- Margaret...

1499
01:25:56.714 --> 01:25:58.672
I don't even believe in God!

1500
01:26:06.985 --> 01:26:08.769
Are you happy? Hmm?

1501
01:26:10.902 --> 01:26:12.947
- I'm so sorry. I did this.
- No, no, no. This is not...

1502
01:26:12.948 --> 01:26:14.426
- I am so sorry.
- No, this is not your fault.

1503
01:26:14.427 --> 01:26:17.299
This is not your fault.
Okay, this is not your fault.

1504
01:26:17.300 --> 01:26:20.041
No, that was everybody else.
That was not...

1505
01:26:20.042 --> 01:26:21.912
- Me.
- No, no, no.

1506
01:26:24.829 --> 01:26:26.396
<i>"Dear Mr. Benedict,</i>

1507
01:26:28.441 --> 01:26:32.402
<i>"what I learned about religion
is that it makes people fight.</i>

1508
01:26:34.882 --> 01:26:37.580
<i>"That every religion
says the same thing.</i>

1509
01:26:37.581 --> 01:26:40.539
<i>"If you pray to God,
he'll listen to you,</i>

1510
01:26:40.540 --> 01:26:42.368
<i>"and help you,
and make things better.</i>

1511
01:26:45.067 --> 01:26:47.546
<i>"But I've prayed and prayed</i>

1512
01:26:47.547 --> 01:26:50.202
<i>"and everything just gets worse."</i>

1513
01:26:55.555 --> 01:26:57.166
Okay.
We'll call you.

1514
01:26:59.820 --> 01:27:01.822
<i>"I don't know anymore,
but I think...</i>

1515
01:27:03.607 --> 01:27:05.652
<i>"that maybe the truth is...</i>

1516
01:27:08.742 --> 01:27:10.135
<i>"there's nobody up there.</i>

1517
01:27:13.312 --> 01:27:15.010
<i>"There's nobody listening.</i>

1518
01:27:18.883 --> 01:27:20.450
<i>"There's only just...</i>

1519
01:27:22.800 --> 01:27:23.931
<i>"me.</i>

1520
01:27:37.032 --> 01:27:40.209
<i>"Sincerely, Margaret Simon."</i>

1521
01:27:46.258 --> 01:27:47.302
Margaret.

1522
01:29:12.127 --> 01:29:14.432
- Hey.
- Hey.

1523
01:29:14.433 --> 01:29:16.131
Wait.
Come here.

1524
01:29:17.828 --> 01:29:19.743
I don't really feel like talking.

1525
01:29:21.092 --> 01:29:22.528
Yeah.
I don't either.

1526
01:29:24.487 --> 01:29:29.492
But, um, I do want to say
sorry for how things went.

1527
01:29:32.103 --> 01:29:36.063
And I know that this past year
has not been easy.

1528
01:29:41.373 --> 01:29:43.070
Want to just sit for a minute?

1529
01:29:57.781 --> 01:30:01.045
Mmm, yeah.
Good idea.

1530
01:30:13.710 --> 01:30:17.148
It gets tiring trying so hard
all the time, doesn't it?

1531
01:30:19.194 --> 01:30:20.238
Yeah.

1532
01:30:55.752 --> 01:30:59.320
- One, two, three. Cheese!
- Cheese!

1533
01:30:59.321 --> 01:31:03.019
Junior High! Whoo!

1534
01:31:03.020 --> 01:31:05.631
Come on, everybody.
Margaret, come on!

1535
01:31:10.506 --> 01:31:11.506
Hey.

1536
01:31:14.074 --> 01:31:15.206
Thanks, Mr. Benedict.

1537
01:31:16.251 --> 01:31:18.469
You're a really good teacher.

1538
01:31:18.470 --> 01:31:20.515
Well, I wouldn't say all that.
You know,

1539
01:31:20.516 --> 01:31:22.952
still trying to iron out some of the kinks.

1540
01:31:22.953 --> 01:31:24.650
No, you were really good.

1541
01:31:26.565 --> 01:31:27.784
I'm glad you felt that way.

1542
01:31:45.541 --> 01:31:46.541
Hey.

1543
01:31:49.632 --> 01:31:50.937
Do you want to come dance?

1544
01:31:53.288 --> 01:31:54.419
Really?

1545
01:31:55.377 --> 01:31:56.377
Yeah.

1546
01:32:09.652 --> 01:32:11.087
Yes!
I knew it!

1547
01:32:11.088 --> 01:32:12.523
You basically already won.

1548
01:32:12.524 --> 01:32:14.438
You've been going for ages.

1549
01:32:14.439 --> 01:32:16.788
- Ages, Gretchen?
- Can I please go?

1550
01:32:16.789 --> 01:32:18.791
Gretchen, quit complaining all the time.

1551
01:32:19.749 --> 01:32:20.924
I'm not complaining.

1552
01:32:26.146 --> 01:32:27.321
Nancy.

1553
01:32:28.497 --> 01:32:29.672
Come on, please?

1554
01:32:35.721 --> 01:32:36.722
I got it!

1555
01:32:52.390 --> 01:32:54.696
Really nice work on the shading, Daniel.

1556
01:32:54.697 --> 01:32:55.914
Thank you.

1557
01:32:55.915 --> 01:32:57.960
I think maybe you could put a wash here

1558
01:32:57.961 --> 01:33:01.660
just to blend that, but I...
It's beautiful.

1559
01:33:07.492 --> 01:33:10.189
- Oh. Hey, Barbara!
- Jan!

1560
01:33:10.190 --> 01:33:12.453
It's so funny to see you.
I was just gonna call you.

1561
01:33:12.454 --> 01:33:14.193
- Oh.
- Can you believe it,

1562
01:33:14.194 --> 01:33:15.586
about the stars?

1563
01:33:15.587 --> 01:33:17.414
- Oh, I know.
- Jeez.

1564
01:33:17.415 --> 01:33:19.982
Well, I guess everything
is a fire hazard these days.

1565
01:33:21.463 --> 01:33:22.985
Anyway, um,

1566
01:33:22.986 --> 01:33:24.160
we're getting committees together

1567
01:33:24.161 --> 01:33:25.509
over at the Junior High

1568
01:33:25.510 --> 01:33:27.032
and I can think of at least three

1569
01:33:27.033 --> 01:33:28.773
that you'd be perfect for.

1570
01:33:28.774 --> 01:33:34.606
Oh, Jan, that sounds great
and I'd love to, but, um...

1571
01:33:36.695 --> 01:33:38.001
I don't want to.

1572
01:33:40.438 --> 01:33:42.570
But thank you for asking me.

1573
01:33:42.571 --> 01:33:45.051
- Yeah.
- And, uh...

1574
01:33:46.183 --> 01:33:47.837
- Have a good day!
- Okay.

1575
01:33:52.711 --> 01:33:54.277
<i>I'm going to write you
so many letters.</i>

1576
01:33:54.278 --> 01:33:56.758
So many letters,
the mailman's going to say,

1577
01:33:56.759 --> 01:33:58.803
"That's it! No more!"

1578
01:33:58.804 --> 01:34:00.588
Okay.

1579
01:34:00.589 --> 01:34:02.764
<i>Oh. Have the best time, honey.</i>

1580
01:34:02.765 --> 01:34:03.982
<i>We'll see you when you get back.</i>

1581
01:34:03.983 --> 01:34:05.070
See you soon, sweetie.

1582
01:34:05.071 --> 01:34:06.463
- Have fun.
- Bye.

1583
01:34:06.464 --> 01:34:07.770
Love you.
Bye!

1584
01:34:10.642 --> 01:34:12.991
- Okay. I think this is it.
- Got it?

1585
01:34:12.992 --> 01:34:14.732
- Then we just have to...
- Wait, wait, wait.

1586
01:34:14.733 --> 01:34:16.038
- ...close it.
- Yeah.

1587
01:34:16.039 --> 01:34:17.866
- Camera, camera, camera.
- Oh, wait.

1588
01:34:17.867 --> 01:34:19.345
- Yes.
- All right.

1589
01:34:19.346 --> 01:34:21.478
Okay. Now, we just
have to close it.

1590
01:34:21.479 --> 01:34:22.958
- Sides. Check the sides.
- Okay, got it?

1591
01:34:22.959 --> 01:34:24.350
- Yeah, yeah. Step on it.
- Ready. Go.

1592
01:34:24.351 --> 01:34:26.744
Oh, my God! Are you okay?

1593
01:34:26.745 --> 01:34:28.050
Whoo. Ah.

1594
01:34:28.051 --> 01:34:30.052
- Just kidding.
- Every time.

1595
01:34:30.053 --> 01:34:31.357
If it's there, I'll take it.

1596
01:34:31.358 --> 01:34:32.881
- Okay.
- Good stuff. There it is.

1597
01:34:32.882 --> 01:34:34.752
Almost like we've done it before.

1598
01:34:34.753 --> 01:34:37.103
Yeah.

1599
01:34:40.019 --> 01:34:41.238
Is it lawn day?

1600
01:34:43.109 --> 01:34:44.110
It is.

1601
01:34:46.765 --> 01:34:48.592
- We haven't paid him yet.
- We haven't.

1602
01:34:48.593 --> 01:34:50.420
No. And if you wanted to go
into the kitchen

1603
01:34:50.421 --> 01:34:51.509
and grab it...

1604
01:34:53.032 --> 01:34:55.948
Yeah. Yeah. Sure.

1605
01:35:05.218 --> 01:35:06.567
Hey. Hey, Moose.

1606
01:35:09.353 --> 01:35:10.614
Here.
Dad says thanks.

1607
01:35:10.615 --> 01:35:12.050
Oh, thank you.
Yeah.

1608
01:35:12.051 --> 01:35:14.488
Uh, well, have a good summer.

1609
01:35:14.489 --> 01:35:16.098
I won't be seeing you for a while.

1610
01:35:16.099 --> 01:35:17.839
Oh, where you going?

1611
01:35:17.840 --> 01:35:20.319
Camp.
New Hampshire. Yeah.

1612
01:35:20.320 --> 01:35:22.147
- Oh.
- Leaving today.

1613
01:35:22.148 --> 01:35:23.454
Well, have fun.

1614
01:35:25.108 --> 01:35:26.109
Thanks.

1615
01:35:27.458 --> 01:35:28.980
And, uh, I don't know.

1616
01:35:28.981 --> 01:35:30.940
Maybe we can hang out when you get back?

1617
01:35:32.202 --> 01:35:33.812
Re... Really?

1618
01:35:34.857 --> 01:35:35.858
Yeah.

1619
01:35:38.034 --> 01:35:40.079
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

1620
01:36:18.596 --> 01:36:19.902
Oh, my God.

1621
01:36:20.946 --> 01:36:22.512
Oh, my God.

1622
01:36:22.513 --> 01:36:24.167
Mom... Mom?

1623
01:36:25.342 --> 01:36:27.386
Mom!
Mom!

1624
01:36:27.387 --> 01:36:29.432
What is it?
What's wrong?

1625
01:36:29.433 --> 01:36:32.697
I got it.
I got my period.

1626
01:36:33.480 --> 01:36:34.656
What?

1627
01:36:38.007 --> 01:36:39.835
- I got it, right?
- Yeah!

1628
01:36:40.879 --> 01:36:43.359
Yeah. Yes.

1629
01:36:43.360 --> 01:36:46.624
Oh, my God.

1630
01:36:51.281 --> 01:36:53.499
I don't know why I'm crying.

1631
01:36:53.500 --> 01:36:55.763
Oh, my goodness.
Wow.

1632
01:36:55.764 --> 01:36:57.982
- Are you okay? Yeah?
- I'm fine. I'm fine.

1633
01:36:57.983 --> 01:37:00.202
- You feel...
- Yep, I'm fine.

1634
01:37:00.203 --> 01:37:02.030
Do you have any cramping or...

1635
01:37:02.031 --> 01:37:03.988
- No. No, no, no. No, I'm fine.
- No?

1636
01:37:03.989 --> 01:37:05.511
I can't believe this is happening to you.

1637
01:37:05.512 --> 01:37:06.687
I don't believe it either.

1638
01:37:06.688 --> 01:37:08.210
You're a woman!

1639
01:37:08.211 --> 01:37:09.472
I'm a woman!

1640
01:37:13.520 --> 01:37:15.391
Okay, um...
Get down to business.

1641
01:37:15.392 --> 01:37:16.479
- We need pads.
- Yeah.

1642
01:37:16.480 --> 01:37:17.698
- Yeah, yeah.
- Yeah.

1643
01:37:17.699 --> 01:37:19.003
I actually bought you some.

1644
01:37:19.004 --> 01:37:20.352
- Really?
- I was going to sneak them

1645
01:37:20.353 --> 01:37:22.398
into your trunk at camp,
you know, just in case.

1646
01:37:22.399 --> 01:37:24.183
But, okay.
One sec.

1647
01:37:25.402 --> 01:37:26.533
Be right there.

1648
01:37:28.274 --> 01:37:29.449
Okay.
So...

1649
01:37:30.886 --> 01:37:32.930
Um, this is how they work.

1650
01:37:32.931 --> 01:37:34.671
- So you just put...
- I know how to do it.

1651
01:37:34.672 --> 01:37:36.542
I've been practicing
in my room for two months.

1652
01:37:36.543 --> 01:37:40.111
- What?
- Yeah.

1653
01:37:40.112 --> 01:37:41.853
- You have? Oh, my...
- Yes. Yes.

1654
01:37:44.421 --> 01:37:45.769
All right.

1655
01:37:45.770 --> 01:37:48.643
Well, then, you're, um...
You don't need me.

1656
01:37:51.080 --> 01:37:52.428
Yeah.

1657
01:37:52.429 --> 01:37:54.300
I'll be right out here.
Okay.

1658
01:38:31.294 --> 01:38:32.904
<i>Are you still there, God?</i>

1659
01:38:33.731 --> 01:38:35.559
<i>It's me, Margaret.</i>

1660
01:38:37.561 --> 01:38:38.649
<i>Thanks.</i>

1661
01:38:39.389 --> 01:38:40.869
<i>Thanks an awful lot.</i>
